WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.968
-Welcome back to "Late Night".

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.269
We're here with Gwen Stefani.

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.505
Often times, on "The Voice",
people will do covers,

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.607
sometimes even covers
of your music.

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:10.410
-That's true.
-Do your ears like hearing it?

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.514
-You know, I get really excited,
but John Legend is known

00:00:15.514 --> 00:00:18.350
to not press his button if
someone does one of his songs.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.719
And we're just kind of like,
"John, just -- you have

00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:21.720
to press your button.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.055
They're doing your song."

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:25.424
And I guess he gets, like, very
scientific about it,

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:26.659
and he just gets overwhelmed.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:31.097
But people have done mine,
not -- I can't say when,

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.733
'cause this hasn't come out yet.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:36.402
But I know one season,
somebody did "Cool",

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:38.838
and I wasn't on that season,
and Blake was like,

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.072
"Oh, my God,
they did your song!"

00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:42.742
And it was just a totally weird
version of it,

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.076
and it's awesome.

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:45.945
I love -- they're always doing
covers on that show.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.246
-It's really great.
-Yeah.

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:48.814
-I was just wondering -- it's so
funny because, obviously,

00:00:48.814 --> 00:00:50.950
you have these intense
relationships with your songs.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.184
I'm wondering when you hear
somebody else do it,

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:53.953
is it, "Oh, that's so nice that
I'm sharing,"

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.287
or is it, "Get your hands
off it"?

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:57.790
-[ Chuckles ] No, I love to hear
them do it,

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.826
it's just that sometimes
I feel like

00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:03.062
because they're so personal,
the lyrics,

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:06.132
and then if they're like
[Vocalizing] like, doing

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.434
all these, like, fancy, like,
vocals on it,

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.537
I'll be like, "Oh, that's so..."

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:14.040
-It wasn't actually what I was
feeling the day I wrote that

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.808
or ever.
-Or, like, they're a way better

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:18.578
singer, so they're, like, making
it, like, different.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:22.148
So, yeah, it's always flatt--
-You're being very diplomatic,

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.917
and I appreciate that.
-But it's very flattering.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.552
-That's nice.
-And it's incredible.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.654
-I want to talk about
your makeup line...

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.255
-Yes, please.
-...GXVE.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.457
And this is really cool, and
you're doing something

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:33.459
even cooler -- this is what the
box will look like.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:35.128
-I was gonna say, "Is there
something in there?"

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:37.062
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.062 --> 00:01:38.731
-I don't think so.
-I feel like we've got

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:43.202
some, like, lip glosses for you.
-Thank you so much.

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:46.806
But talk about GXVE Community,
'cause this is a really

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:48.441
nice partnership thing
you're doing.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:52.745
Well, I mean, back in the day, I
did a lot of different things,

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.047
but I wanted to, when my life
kind of fell apart --

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:58.117
I don't know people know, but I
had a really, like, bad chapter.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.420
And I just was trying to figure
out what I'm gonna do

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.820
for the rest of my life,
you know?

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.723
Even my parents were like,
"Don't do anything."

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.991
And I was like, "But I kind of
want to do something creative

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:08.628
still," so I've always been
into makeup.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:11.564
I was a makeup artist way back
in the day.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:14.834
I worked at the counter, and
I did makeovers on people.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.903
And I just love the way makeup
makes people feel

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:20.773
and how powerful it can be
and just confidence

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.308
and all the things
that it brings.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.810
And also just an art, like,
expressing yourself.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:28.080
So I felt like people -- there
was a really big community

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.317
out there already of people that
are just, like, makeup fanatics

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.585
like I am.

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.488
So I started the line, but I
wanted it to be more

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:38.424
not just about the makeup,
but also about the community

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:41.126
and giving people a chance
to be part of something

00:02:41.126 --> 00:02:42.562
that I've done.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.863
And, like, literally, they can
make, like, sell the makeup

00:02:44.863 --> 00:02:47.733
and make money off
of the collection that they get.

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:50.169
So it's, like, it's just one
of these things where

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:51.704
just take it another
step further.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:54.740
Like, you could either work
at the counter,

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.775
but you can do it from home,
and you can, like, build up

00:02:56.775 --> 00:02:59.411
your followers, you can have
your own platform,

00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:01.246
you can share the makeup.

00:03:01.246 --> 00:03:03.582
It's like they're already doing
it, but it's kind of

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:05.417
making a place for them to all
come together.

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:07.686
-That's really nice, and you,
I would imagine

00:03:07.686 --> 00:03:09.789
back in the early days,
obviously, it's all changed now,

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:15.027
but you are doing the kind of
maybe grittier music venues

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:16.829
with those smaller green rooms.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.631
And you were doing
your own makeup.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.366
-I've done my own makeup
my whole life,

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:23.035
and, you know, only until
recently I got to work

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:24.904
with amazing people
and learn so much,

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.272
and I'm still learning.
And that's what's so fun

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.440
about the community,
everybody sharing.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.643
Like, we, back in the day,
we didn't have that,

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.745
but now, we have access
to all this information

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:36.583
and tutorials and great makeup.

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.918
And so -- but back in the day,
I was in a compact on a bus

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:41.387
with, like, all guys around me,
and the bus is moving.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.588
-[ Laughs ]
-And I -- you know,

00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:43.722
it was very challenging.

00:03:43.722 --> 00:03:45.992
But I'm actually nervous talking
about this,

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.727
'cause it's such a big dream
of mine.

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:49.595
I've been working on this
for over four years.

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:52.064
Announcing it, like -- it's one
thing to come out

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:54.000
with a makeup line, to come out
with this community

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.901
where people can actually
partner with me

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:58.471
and be like, "You guys, you've
been, exchanging love

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:00.973
all this time, and now you're
gonna get paid for it."

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:03.576
Like, it's kind of exciting
for me to, like, be talking

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.077
to you about it.
I'm like, "Aah!" [ Chuckles ]

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:06.779
-Well, it's really --
-I hope I'm explaining

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.047
it right. [ Laughs ]
-I think you're doing

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.849
a great job.
And I think that's really

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:13.785
exciting, and I think people
probably can't wait to

00:04:13.785 --> 00:04:15.154
get involved with it.

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:17.456
And it is just always such
a pleasure to have you here,

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:19.925
and in person,
better than any other way.

00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:21.360
Thank you so much --
-You're better in person, too.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.428
-Okay, thank you.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.330
You guys, Gwen Stefani!

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.565
"The Voice" premiers
September 19th at 8 P.M.

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:28.001
on NBC.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:30.903
And GXVE Beauty is available
at Sephora and gxvebeauty.com.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.572
We'll be right back
with Grant Morrison.

